        "Structure": {
          "Structure_Text": {
            "original": "SiCp/Al composite consists of Al matrix and SiC particles (6H-SiC polytype). XRD spectrum confirms phase composition. TEM reveals amorphous layer of ~40 nm on machined surface, with subsurface defects including SiC particle fracture, micro-cracks, dislocations, and stacking faults at SiC/Al interface. No debonding at two-phase interface. 6H-SiC lattice spacing 2.36 Å, plane index (103); Al matrix lattice spacing 2.02 Å, plane index (200).",
            "simplified": "Matrix: Al (FCC, a spacing 2.02 Å, plane (200)); Reinforcement: 6H-SiC (HCP, a spacing 2.36 Å, plane (103)); Amorphous layer ~40 nm on machined surface; Subsurface defects: particle fracture, micro-crack, dislocations, stacking faults"
          },
